  <title id="bdl10overconfidencergpr-title">Predictive confidence of MAP, Laplace and RGPR on two moons</title>
  <desc id="bdl10overconfidencergpr-desc">Three square panels over the input square from minus 5 to 5 show the confidence of a ReLU network on a two-moons data set, with the decision boundary drawn as a line. In the MAP panel nearly the whole plane is shaded dark, meaning confidence close to 1 everywhere except along the boundary. In the Laplace panel the shading fades with distance from the data. In the RGPR panel the shading is light everywhere away from the data. A fourth panel plots the maximum confidence along a ray against the distance from the origin on a logarithmic axis from 1 to 100: the MAP curve rises to 1, the Laplace curve levels off below 1, and the RGPR curve falls back toward 0.5. A colour bar beside it maps the shading to confidence values from 0.5 to 1.0.</desc>
  <defs>
    <marker id="bdl10overconfidencergpr-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
      <path class="arrowhead" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" />
    </marker>
  </defs>
